he frog-folk","guarded by a hydra that has not been seen in a century","where the elves once grew their moon-lilies","a vast reed sea with a floating market at its heart","where the mist never fully lifts","said to hide the lost crown of a marsh king","where every pool shows a different sky","home to herons who are said to speak","crossed by stilt-walkers and their long-legged boats","where a drowned temple surfaces in dry summers","a wetland so wide it has its own weather","ruled by a council of ancient turtles","where travellers follow the glow-moths or get lost","a green maze of willow, water and old magic","where the river forgets which way it was going","the last refuge of the swamp dragons"],"haunted":["where lights move across the water on still nights","where a drowned church bell still rings at midnight","a bog that gives back what it takes, a hundred years late","where no birds sing","where travellers hear their names called from the reeds","where the mist rises in the shape of people","a mire that has swallowed three roads and a village","where a pale lady walks the causeway at dusk","where the hounds will not go","where footprints appear on the mud with no one to make them","avoided by locals after the sun goes down","where the old gibbet still creaks in the wind","a black bog that never freezes, even in deep winter","where a phantom ferryman waits for one last passenger","where the candle-lights lead the unwary into deep water","where the dead of an old battle were never buried","where the cold creeps into your bones and stays","a silent fen where even the frogs fall quiet","where something large breathes under the surface","where every lantern you carry burns blue","said to be the doorway to the land of the dead","where a sunken village shows its rooftops in drought","where the willows lean in to listen","where the fog comes in faster than you can run"],"fen":["a wet alder wood where the old drove road sinks out of sight","drained by Dutch engineers and slowly winning back its water","cut for peat since the days of the abbey","where the reed-cutters still work in winter","a flat, wide land under an enormous sky","where the river floods the water meadows every winter","home to bitterns that boom in the spring","crossed by a single raised causeway","where eels were once paid as rent","where the fen skaters race when the lodes freeze","an island of higher ground with a church on it","grazed by cattle in summer and drowned in winter","where the windpumps creak on the dykes","a moss of bog cotton, sundews and wandering curlews","where the drains run straight to the horizon","a wild corner the drainers never quite managed to tame","where the villagers still hold rights to cut turf","patrolled by marsh harriers on summer afternoons","where an old smugglers' track crosses the reeds","a nature reserve loved by birdwatchers","where the black soil grows the best celery in the county","flooded on purpose each winter for the wildfowl","where a buried bog oak was dug up the size of a ship","a carr of willow and alder alive with warblers"],"bayou":["where the cypress knees stick up like old men's fingers","heavy with Spanish moss and the smell of rain","where the gators sun themselves on the mudbanks","reached only by pirogue","where the fishing camps stand on stilts","where the crawfish traps are checked at dawn","where an old fiddler is said to play on summer nights","where the fireflies come out in their millions","a backwater the maps never quite got right","where the herons stand still as statues","where a hurricane once moved the whole channel","where the bullfrogs drown out the radio","home to a family that has fished it for six generations","where the rougarou is said to walk at night","where the water is the colour of strong tea","lined with tupelo and bald cypress","where a sunken paddle steamer rests in the mud","where the cottonmouths keep folk on the boardwalk","a slow brown water full of catfish","where the old trapper's cabin still stands","where the mosquitoes are the size of hummingbirds, or so they say","where the egrets roost in their hundreds at dusk","where you can hear the dance hall from a mile away","quiet enough to hear a turtle slip off a log"],"witchy":["where the best toadstools grow, if you know where to look","where a coven meets beneath the full moon","where the mist smells faintly of peppermint and smoke","where an old witch keeps a cottage on hen's legs","where the frogs croak in rhyme","where the water bubbles like a cauldron on cold days","where every herb for every potion can be found","home to a very large and very grumpy toad","where the black cats gather at dusk","where a wise woman sells charms from a boat","where wishes thrown into the pools sometimes come true","where the will-o'-the-wisps run errands for the witches","where the moon looks bigger than anywhere else","where broomsticks are cut from the best willow","where the sundews are said to eat more than flies","where a cauldron the size of a cottage sank long ago","where the herons keep the witches' secrets","where a spell went wrong and never quite wore off","where you should always say please to the reeds","where the hags hold their great spring market","where the steam rises green on Midsummer's Eve","where a gingerbread hut sinks a little more each year","where the newts are all slightly enchanted","where the mandrakes are dug up only with earmuffs on"]}}}